<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The mark as a silhouette, for the themed-icon layer.

  ⚠️ ITS OWN FILE, AND IT HAS TO BE. `ic_launcher.xml` could point its `monochrome` layer at the
  foreground beside it, and the result would be a block: a monochrome layer is re-tinted to one flat
  ink, so the three strengths the foreground draws the segments in all collapse together and the
  cuts between them — the only thing that gives the shape structure — disappear.

  ⚠️ THE PALE TRIANGLE IS NOT DRAWN, AND THAT IS HOW THE CUT SURVIVES. The three segments are
  disjoint, so leaving one out leaves a hole in exactly its shape rather than needing a mask a
  vector drawable cannot express. What is left reads as the mark with its corner open, which is what
  the coloured version reads as at a glance.

  ⚠️ #FFFFFF IS NOT THE COLOUR IT WILL BE. A monochrome layer is re-tinted by the launcher to the
  system theme; only its alpha is read here.

  ⚠️ THE PATHS ARE `ic_launcher_foreground.xml`'s, unchanged. The mapping from the model's box into
  this canvas is written out there.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M54,75.42L76,61.53L76,32.58L54,46.47Z" />

    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M54,46.47L32,32.58L32,61.53Z" />
</vector>
